---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import AnchorHeading from '../components/AnchorHeading.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import atlasManifest from '../../public/atlas/data/catalog/index.json';

const recordCount = atlasManifest.totalRecords.toLocaleString('en-US');
const geographicCount = atlasManifest.geographicRecords.toLocaleString('en-US');
const frameCount = atlasManifest.flyoverCameraFrames.toLocaleString('en-US');
const layerCount = atlasManifest.layers.length;
const description =
  'Explore retained location records with their source evidence: full cell identities, estimates, coverage grids, infrastructure records, and virtual Flyover resources. Research preview.';
---

<Base title="Local Evidence Atlas" description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  </Fragment>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Research preview"
    title="Location records, with the evidence attached."
    lead="See what each point represents, where it came from, and which connections the evidence supports."
  >
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/atlas/records/index.html" class="btn btn-primary">
        Explore all {recordCount} records <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
      </a>
      <a href="/research/local-evidence-atlas/" class="btn btn-ghost">
        Read the case study
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-ink-3">
      This research preview retains real technical data and its evidence limits. The original unredacted evidence stays
      private and unchanged; personal hardware and access information is excluded from this separate derivative.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="container-x pt-10" aria-labelledby="atlas-scope">
    <h2 id="atlas-scope" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
      A record count is not a tower count.
    </h2>
    <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card p-5">
        <dt class="text-sm text-ink-3">Retained source records</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{recordCount}</dd>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-2">
          {geographicCount} have display coordinates; {atlasManifest.unmappedRecords} remain unplotted.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-5">
        <dt class="text-sm text-ink-3">Distinct source layers</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{layerCount}</dd>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-2">
          Returned estimates, grid context, public infrastructure, and virtual map resources retain their different
          roles.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-5">
        <dt class="text-sm text-ink-3">Verified identity-to-site links</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">0</dd>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-2">
          A nearby pole, a shared PCI, or precise-looking coordinates do not establish an antenna location.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="container-x grid gap-4 pt-8 md:grid-cols-2" aria-labelledby="atlas-views">
    <h2 id="atlas-views" class="sr-only">
      Choose an evidence view
    </h2>
    <article class="card flex flex-col items-start p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Complete catalog</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Follow every retained record.</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-2">
        Search full LTE ECI and NR NCI values, TAC, PCI, carrier names, places, and public site identifiers. Inspect
        complete selected source fields. Coverage wire and all {frameCount} virtual camera frames load when requested.
      </p>
      <a href="/atlas/records/index.html" class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-accent">
        Open the full map and catalog <Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />
      </a>
    </article>
    <article class="card flex flex-col items-start p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Downtown Los Angeles case</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">One identity. Two source estimates.</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-2">
        Compare the actual returned coordinates for NR 310/260, TAC 3960320, NCI 7587668269. Their centers are 69.38 m
        apart. Neither an assigned PCI nor a physical installation has been independently established.
      </p>
      <a href="/atlas/preview/index.html" class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-accent">
        Inspect the exact NR comparison <Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />
      </a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container-x pt-12">
    <div class="prose-readme max-w-[48rem]">
      <AnchorHeading id="meaning">Keep the source role attached.</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        A returned LTE, NR, or Wi-Fi position is a service estimate. A coverage-grid center represents an area and its
        network/channel context. A City pole or permit address is an administrative record. Flyover anchors and camera
        paths describe virtual map content. Their presence does not establish a visit, a device connection, or a
        personal movement timeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        Carrier labels explain network codes: 310/260 is associated with T-Mobile, 310/410 with AT&amp;T, and 311/480
        with Verizon. Assignment dates and unresolved codes remain visible. Names do not identify antenna ownership or a
        subscriber’s retail plan. PCI searches qualify the same source posting by network, radio, and channel; they do
        not join a full cell identity to nearby coverage.
      </p>
      <AnchorHeading id="method">Read the research before connecting the dots.</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        The <a href="/research/local-evidence-atlas/">case study</a> explains the acquisition sources, native parser
        evidence, exact identity comparison, remaining gaps, and limits of interpretation. The interactive views render
        their geography locally, using retained coordinates and generalized land shapes. They make no third-party
        runtime requests and do not request your location or device access.
      </p>
      <p>
        Observation time is unknown for the mapped rows. Provider database dates, permit dates, and acquisition dates
        remain distinct. Original NAD83 planned coordinates stay documentary and unplotted. Original evidence and
        preservation receipts remain separate from this research derivative.
      </p>
      <AnchorHeading id="source-use">Source attribution and reuse limits</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        OpenCellID-derived measurements are attributed to{' '}
        <a href="https://opencellid.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          OpenCellID
        </a>
        , under{' '}
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          CC BY-SA 4.0
        </a>
        , via the mcc-mnc.org mirror. Selection, normalized labels, and added interpretations are changes; returned
        coordinates retain their source digits. This credit does not license the mixed collection as a whole. Apple-feed
        and other source-specific reuse questions remain unresolved. No independently verified vendor license grant or
        endorsement is asserted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/atlas/DATA-NOTICES.md">source and data notices</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/atlas/LICENSE.txt">scoped code license</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/atlas/data/catalog/index.json">complete dataset manifest</a>, and{' '}
        <a href="/atlas/README.md">canonical article source</a>. The separate static explorer carries its own local-only
        Content Security Policy; the main website’s policy is unchanged.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
